O R D E R




 BEFORE:  GRIFFIN, THAPAR, and NALBANDIAN, Circuit Judges.


 The court received a petition for rehearing en banc.  The original panel has rev iewed the petition
for rehearing and concludes that the issues raised in the petition were fully consi dered upon the original
submission and decision of the case.  The petition then was circulated to the ful l court.  No judge has
requested a vote on the suggestion for rehearing en banc.
 Therefore, the petition is denied.



      ENTERED BY ORDER OF THE COURT





